    "updated_at": "2019-04-29T16:10:37Z",
    "body": "In the meeting a point was brought up that you could not necessarily rely on a marker inserted after `</template>` due to dynamic content insertion, but it seems that'd equally apply to the contents of a template, unless that is somehow magic. So I think @domenic is correct and there shouldn't be any special casing here. (I do think we should have declarative shadow trees, but probably not this way.)",
